  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institute of Participatory Devpt - MADCA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Malindi District Cultural Association (MADCA) has been in the fight against the killings of the elderly for a decade now, having established two rescue centres in the county with a current population of 39 elders has not been able to contain the situation as more elders are endangered in their homes. There are those who are held in the rescue centres however many more are suffocating and waiting for their days as they are a target of their tormentors. The local leadership; politicians, religious leaders, county and national governments among others have not shown interest in the killings of the elderly, making this special segment of the society vulnerable. The fight against elderly killings has been seen to be the role of MADCA by all other institutions. MADCA in this new initiative partners with Institute of Participatory Development-Kulamusana (IPD-K) calling for all key stakeholders to collaborate in the fight against the mass killings of the elderly. The project will engage strategic stakeholders for a joint and stronger voice, inthe fight against/eradicating the menace of the killings of the elderly in Kilifi County. The project will specifically; Organize stakeholders around security matters i.e., civil society, politicians, religious leadersamong others, train 10 song composers and record music by November; conduct four radio talk show sessions; conduct outreach programs; conduct radio talk shows to bring leaders in discussions i.e., government, politicians, academicians.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="90">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INSTITUTE OF PARTICIPATORY DEVELOPM</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Institute of Participatory Development-Kulamusana (IPD-K) is a local based organisation started and established by natives of the region. In the last two decades of its operation, the organisation has blended well with the people as it has used culture in project implementation and music has been  a useful tool to pass change messages to the people. Additionally, the organization has a well established network and is identified with the people as an organisation that blends well with the culture of the people within the locality hence the implementation of any new projects can be implemented with community support.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
